Subject: [PATCH 05/12] refactor(chat): turn preparation becomes
 chat_turn_context.build_turn_context
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Third step of the split. Everything stream_chat did before the first
provider call — project scope for billing, the Agent plan and its
non-generating short-circuit, the Code Interpreter capacity lease and
heartbeat, LiteLLM kwargs, tool / profile / memory / project-context
augmentation, cache breakpoints, workspace inventory, the persister — is
now `build_turn_context(db, body, resolved, ...)` returning a
`TurnContext` (or a `NonGeneratingReply` whose frames stream_chat yields).

`CapacityLease` replaces three closures: it owns the permit, the budget
hold id, the `lost` event and the heartbeat task, and `abandon(reason)`
is the one place that gives both resources back when preparation fails
(previously two copy-pasted `except BaseException` blocks).
`adaptive_openrouter_extra_body`, `resolve_private_mode_for_memory` and
`resolve_session_project_id` move along with it.

Preflight stays in stream_chat (build requires a resolved context); the
streaming loop still works on plain locals unpacked from the context, so
this commit changes no loop code. Tests that patched preparation
collaborators on proxy_service now patch chat_turn_context; two test
`with (...)` blocks with >20 context managers hit CPython's static
nesting limit and became ExitStack loops.

stream_chat: 1194 -> 795 lines, CC 101 (was ~150). proxy_service 1658
lines. 1371 tests; mypy baseline shrinks by one; vulture/ruff clean.

